Export the reverse contraction of a host functional's surface adjoints.

moist's models hand their components' surface adjoints (dE/d position, normal,
area, width, switching factor, curvature) to the cavity, whose reverse pass
turns them into the nuclear gradient (get_surface_gradient) and, on a
density-backed level set, into density weights (get_surface_response).  Only
the field route of the electronic half was public
(moist_contract_surface_lsf_weights, without the area and integration-weight
channels).  This exports both, for an energy the host computes itself on the
surface (tautomator's and psi4-swig-pcm's nonelectrostatic terms):

  moist_contract_cavity_surface_gradient  every channel -> dE/dR
  moist_contract_cavity_surface_density   every channel -> (w_rho, w_grad_rho,
                                          w_hess_rho), dS/drho folded in

with Python wrappers (library.contract_cavity_surface_gradient/_density) and
DROP cavity methods (contract_surface_gradient/_density).  Nothing existing
changes.

diff --git a/include/moist.h b/include/moist.h
index 6e9be9b..3cff8a8 100644
--- a/include/moist.h
+++ b/include/moist.h
@@ -1604,6 +1604,58 @@ moist_contract_surface_lsf_weights_extended(
